# Security

- Never log secrets, access tokens, payment references, or personally sensitive information.
- Never hard-code credentials, tokens, or user IDs. Use environment variables and the auth adapter.
- Scope every read and write by `userId`.
- Do not introduce real payment processors.
- Local demo identity stays behind the auth adapter. Do not treat demo identity as production auth.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
console.log("token", accessToken, "pay", paymentRef, "email", email);
await invoices.get({ invoiceId });

// ✅ GOOD
logger.info("invoice fetched", { invoiceId, userId });
await invoices.get({ userId, invoiceId });
```
